# Secret files

Files agents must never open, print or copy. The secret guard hook (`.claude/hooks/guard-secrets.py`) blocks the
kit defaults below, plus every glob you add here. One glob per bullet, in backticks. A glob with a `/` matches the
path from the project root; one without matches the file name anywhere.

Adding a line here tightens the guard. Removing a default does nothing: the defaults are built into the hook, and
loosening it is an owner decision (gate G7). Templates such as `.env.example` are never blocked.

## Kit defaults (always enforced)

This section documents the built-in list. The hook doesn't read it, so editing it changes nothing.

- `.env`
- `.env.*` (not `.env.example`, `.env.sample`, `.env.template`, `.env.dist`)
- `*.pem`
- `*.key`
- `*.p8`
- `*.p12`
- `*.pfx`
- `id_rsa*` (not `.pub`)
- `id_ed25519*` (not `.pub`)
- `id_ecdsa*` (not `.pub`)
- `.claude/notify.env`
- `.netrc`
- `.npmrc` and `.pypirc`, when they hold a token or password

## This project

Add this project's own secret files below, for example `config/credentials.yml` or `*.tfvars`.

